The rustyecon atlas: licence of the data in data/atlas/ (2026-09-27)

The atlas database, gb.atlas.ron, is derived from OpenStreetMap data and from data of the
Historic County Borders Project. It is made available under the Open Data Commons Open Database
License (ODbL) v1.0:

    https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

In short, and the licence's own text governs: you may copy, distribute and adapt it, provided
you attribute it as ATTRIBUTION says, offer any adapted database you use publicly under the
ODbL, and, if you distribute it with technical restrictions, also make an unrestricted copy
available.

preview.png is a Produced Work from the atlas under the ODbL. It carries its attribution on the
image and may be used under the same notice.

This licence covers the data files only. The build script (build_atlas.py), requirements.txt and
the Rust code that reads the atlas (crates/worldgen) are code, under the repository's terms; the
ODbL does not reach them (docs/GUI.md §6, ruling 3).

The sources' own terms, which the atlas respects:

- Historic County Borders Project (Historic Counties Trust), UK Definition B. Its README makes
  the data free "for all personal, educational, non-commercial and commercial use", with no
  permission needed, and asks for an acknowledgement, which ATTRIBUTION gives.
- OpenStreetMap: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, under the ODbL 1.0
  (https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright). The riding lines of Yorkshire come from it, which
  is why the atlas as a whole is under the ODbL.
